{"tool_name":"correct_bacode","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"correct_bacode","home":"https://github.com/rikenbit/correct_barcode/","license":"MIT","summary":"The command corrects a DNA sequencing error of cell barcoding containing RT primer sets for Quartz-Seq2 which one of a high throughput single-cell RNA-sequencing.","addition_date":"2018-08-15T10:17:36Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:28:43.920357Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:correct_bacode","credit":[{"email":"itoshi.nikaido@riken.jp","name":"Itoshi Nikaido","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/rikenbit/correct_barcode/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"RNA-Seq analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3680"}]}],"name":"correct_bacode","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-018-1407-3","metadata":{"abstract":"High-throughput single-cell RNA-seq methods assign limited unique molecular identifier (UMI) counts as gene expression values to single cells from shallow sequence reads and detect limited gene counts. We thus developed a high-throughput single-cell RNA-seq method, Quartz-Seq2, to overcome these issues. Our improvements in the reaction steps make it possible to effectively convert initial reads to UMI counts, at a rate of 30-50%, and detect more genes. To demonstrate the power of Quartz-Seq2, we analyzed approximately 10,000 transcriptomes from in vitro embryonic stem cells and an in vivo stromal vascular fraction with a limited number of reads.","authors":[{"name":"Danno H."},{"name":"Ebisawa M."},{"name":"Hayashi T."},{"name":"Kurisaki A."},{"name":"Nikaido I."},{"name":"Sasagawa Y."},{"name":"Takada H."},{"name":"Tanaka K."}],"citationCount":94,"date":"2018-03-09T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"Quartz-Seq2: A high-th